# RBOPS state — committed markers are the state store.
!phases/*/
phases/*/*
!phases/*/PROMPT.md
!phases/*/REPORT.md
!phases/*/FINDINGS.md
!phases/*/.done
!phases/*/.failed
!phases/*/.deferred
!phases/*/.blocked
!phases/*/.checkpoint
!phases/*/.recovered
!phases/*/.conflict
!phases/*/.attempts
!phases/*/.deferred_attempts
# Manual-finish records: a human closing a phase writes MANUAL-FINISH.md, and a
# human-ordered retry writes RETRY-NOTE.md. Both are state the next tick must
# be able to read (why is this done? why was this unblocked?), so they are
# committed like any other phase record. Without these two lines `git add -A`
# silently drops them — which is how phase-032's MANUAL-FINISH.md ended up
# written to disk but never committed.
!phases/*/MANUAL-FINISH.md
!phases/*/RETRY-NOTE.md
!phases/.stop

# Compiled context + prompts are large; the audit record is kept, the ctx is not.
logs/*.ctx
logs/*.prompt

# Secrets — never commit
.env
.env.*
*.key
*.pem
*.keystore
secrets/

# Rust / redblue artifacts
target/
**/*.rs.bk
*.rbc
redblue/

# Editors / OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
.idea/
.vscode/